# Canonical route: the Healing Potions tab where the page offers one
# (1-75, 90-150), since it is the cheaper path when buying everything and
# the route Polestar's own generated guide does not take; the Bandages tab
# is named in each section's tip with its material list, for players who
# already hold the cloth. Expert (150-225) and Artisan (225-300) are
# bandage-only on the page, except the 275-300 Major Healing Potion
# alternative, which is a tip at 260-290.
#
# Spell/item ids resolved from the Forever client tables (build
# 1.60.1.70532, SkillLineAbility.csv + SpellName.csv + SpellReagents.csv),
# each cross-checked against the page's own material lists:
#   Minor Healing Potion 1244431, Simple Poultice 1259342,
#   Healing Potion 1244433, Heavy Runecloth Bandage 18630,
#   Bottle of Dalaran Noir 2723.
# Note: the reference data names item 2723 "Bottle of Pinot Noir" (its
# Classic name); the Forever client tables call it "Bottle of Dalaran
# Noir", and the Simple Poultice recipe lists 2723 as a reagent, so 2723
# is the right id either way.
guide forever-professions/first-aid
title First Aid 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section First Aid 1-75

step Learn First Aid
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip First Aid takes no profession slot, so every character can learn it. Nissa Firestone in Ironforge teaches Apprentice First Aid, at any character level. In Forever, First Aid also makes the healing potions that used to be Alchemy recipes, and this guide brews them where they are cheaper than bandages.
  train First Aid Apprentice npc 5150

step Learn First Aid
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip First Aid takes no profession slot, so every character can learn it. Arnok in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice First Aid, at any character level. In Forever, First Aid also makes the healing potions that used to be Alchemy recipes, and this guide brews them where they are cheaper than bandages.
  train First Aid Apprentice npc 3373

step First Aid 1-75: Auction House
  tip What the potions take that the Auction House sells: 86 Peacebloom. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2447 x86

step First Aid 1-75: herbs
  tip Peacebloom is the starter herb: pick it in any starting zone while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2447 x86 anywhere gather Herbalism 1

step First Aid 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Mild Spices come from Cooking supply vendors and Empty Vials from Alchemy supply vendors, in any capital and most starting zones.
  buy 2678 x86 nearest
  buy 3371 x86 nearest

step Minor Healing Potion (1-75)
  tip Minor Healing Potion is taught with Apprentice First Aid: 86 brews take you to 75. Bandages instead, if you already hold the cloth: 50 Linen Bandage (50 Linen Cloth) to 40, then 47 Heavy Linen Bandage (94 Linen Cloth) to 75.
  learn 1244431 "Minor Healing Potion"
  craft 1244431 "Minor Healing Potion" until 75

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman

section First Aid 75-90

step Journeyman First Aid
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Journeyman First Aid raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and no character level. Nissa Firestone in Ironforge teaches it.
  train First Aid Journeyman npc 5150

step Journeyman First Aid
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Journeyman First Aid raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and no character level. Arnok in Orgrimmar teaches it.
  train First Aid Journeyman npc 3373

step Heavy Linen Bandage: Auction House
  tip What Heavy Linen Bandage takes that the Auction House sells: 26 Linen Cloth. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2589 x26

step Heavy Linen Bandage: cloth
  tip Linen Cloth drops from humanoids of level 5-20: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2589 x26 anywhere gather levels 5-20

step Heavy Linen Bandage (75-80)
  tip Heavy Linen Bandage, 13 crafts to 80. Any First Aid trainer teaches it from skill 40. Bandages need no fire: craft them anywhere.
  learn 3276 "Heavy Linen Bandage"
  craft 3276 "Heavy Linen Bandage" until 80

step Wool Bandage: Auction House
  tip What Wool Bandage takes that the Auction House sells: 12 Wool Cloth. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2592 x12

step Wool Bandage: cloth
  tip Wool Cloth drops from humanoids of level 15-30: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2592 x12 anywhere gather levels 15-30

step Wool Bandage (80-90)
  tip Wool Bandage, 12 crafts to 90. Any First Aid trainer teaches it from skill 80.
  learn 3277 "Wool Bandage"
  craft 3277 "Wool Bandage" until 90

section First Aid 90-125

step First Aid 90-125: Auction House
  tip What the poultices take that the Auction House sells: 54 Spider Ichor. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 3174 x54

step First Aid 90-125: vendor goods
  tip Mild Spices come from Cooking supply vendors and Bottles of Dalaran Noir from barkeeps, in any capital city.
  buy 2678 x54 nearest
  buy 2723 x54 nearest

step Simple Poultice (90-125)
  tip Simple Poultice, 54 brews to 125: Spider Ichor, Mild Spices and a Bottle of Dalaran Noir each. Bandages instead, if you already hold the cloth: 40 Wool Bandage (40 Wool Cloth) to 115, then Heavy Wool Bandage on to 150.
  learn 1259342 "Simple Poultice"
  craft 1259342 "Simple Poultice" until 125

section First Aid 125-150

step First Aid 125-150: Auction House
  tip What the potions take that the Auction House sells: 31 Bruiseweed. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2453 x31

step First Aid 125-150: herbs
  tip Bruiseweed grows in mid-level zones: pick it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2453 x31 anywhere gather Herbalism 75

step First Aid 125-150: vendor goods
  tip Hot Spices come from Cooking supply vendors and Leaded Vials from Alchemy supply vendors. Starting-zone vendors do not sell either: buy them in a capital city.
  buy 2692 x31 nearest
  buy 3372 x31 nearest

step Healing Potion (125-150)
  tip Healing Potion, 31 brews to 150: Bruiseweed, Hot Spices and a Leaded Vial each. Bandages instead, if you already hold the cloth: 51 Heavy Wool Bandage (102 Wool Cloth) from 115 to 150.
  learn 1244433 "Healing Potion"
  craft 1244433 "Healing Potion" until 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert

section First Aid 150-180

step Expert First Aid
  only Alliance
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Expert First Aid raises the cap to 225. It is a book, Expert First Aid - Under Wraps, sold by Deneb Walker in the Arathi Highlands. The book has no level requirement: you only need First Aid 125. Buy the Heavy Silk and Mageweave Bandage manuals from him while you are there; you read them at 180 and 210. Learn Silk Bandage from your trainer before you leave: it is the last recipe the trainers teach.
  train First Aid Expert npc 2805
  buy 16112 x1 nearest
  buy 16113 x1 nearest

step Expert First Aid
  only Horde
  zone Dustwallow Marsh
  tip Expert First Aid raises the cap to 225. It is a book, Expert First Aid - Under Wraps, sold by Balai Lok'Wein in Dustwallow Marsh. The book has no level requirement: you only need First Aid 125. Buy the Heavy Silk and Mageweave Bandage manuals from him while you are there; you read them at 180 and 210. Learn Silk Bandage from your trainer before you leave: it is the last recipe the trainers teach.
  train First Aid Expert npc 13476
  buy 16112 x1 nearest
  buy 16113 x1 nearest

